00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:08,170
Music

3
00:00:08,190 --> 00:00:12,250
Narrator: What safeguards our solar system...

4
00:00:12,270 --> 00:00:16,320
is our star.

5
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:20,390
The sun provides a shield, stretching beyond the last

6
00:00:20,410 --> 00:00:24,440
planet in its orbit: a force field that deflects these

7
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:28,480
"cosmic rays." But these

8
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:32,510
"solar winds" can be dangerous too,

9
00:00:32,530 --> 00:00:36,520
especially during outbursts called coronal mass ejections.

10
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:40,640
Want a vision of earth gone

11
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:44,740
wrong? Just look at what solar storms do our

12
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:48,840
sister planet, Venus. They strip away lighter

13
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:52,920
elements in its upper atmosphere, hydrogen, oxygen

14
00:00:52,940 --> 00:00:57,000
and the molecule they form: water.

15
00:00:57,020 --> 00:01:01,070
What's left is a witch's brew of noxious

16
00:01:01,090 --> 00:01:05,130
chemicals including thick sulfurous clouds.

17
00:01:05,150 --> 00:01:09,180
How has Earth avoided the grim fate of Venus?

18
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:13,220
We can see the answer as the solar storm

19
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:17,240
approaches Earth.

20
00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:21,250
Music

21
00:01:21,270 --> 00:01:25,360
Our planet has a protective shield

22
00:01:25,380 --> 00:01:29,470
all it's own-- A powerful magnetic field

23
00:01:29,490 --> 00:01:33,560
generated deep within its core.

24
00:01:33,580 --> 00:01:37,650
In fact, that's just our first line of

25
00:01:37,670 --> 00:01:41,720
defense. Much of the solar energy that gets through

26
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:45,790
is reflected back to space by clouds, ice,

27
00:01:45,810 --> 00:01:49,840
and snow. The energy that Earth absorbs

28
00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:53,880
is just enough to power a remarkable planetary

29
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:57,900
engine: the climate.

30
00:01:57,920 --> 00:02:01,910
It's set in motion

31
00:02:01,930 --> 00:02:05,990
by the unevenness of solar heating, due in part to the

32
00:02:06,010 --> 00:02:10,070
cycles of day and night, and the seasons that cause warm

33
00:02:10,090 --> 00:02:14,140
tropical winds to blow toward the poles and cold

34
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:18,200
polar air toward the equator.

35
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:22,260
Wind currents

36
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:26,300
drive surface ocean currents.

37
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:30,340
This computer simulation shows the

38
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:34,370
Gulf Stream winding its way along the coast of North America.

39
00:02:34,390 --> 00:02:38,390
Music

40
00:02:38,410 --> 00:02:42,400
Music

41
00:02:42,420 --> 00:02:46,480
Music

42
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:50,550
This great ocean river carries enough heat energy

43
00:02:50,570 --> 00:02:54,620
to power the industrial world a hundred times

44
00:02:54,640 --> 00:02:58,670
over. It breaks down

45
00:02:58,690 --> 00:03:02,720
in massive world pools that spread warm tropical

46
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:06,770
waters over northern seas.

47
00:03:06,790 --> 00:03:10,800
Music

48
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:14,820
Below the surface they mix

49
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:18,840
with cold deep currents that swirl around

50
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:22,930
under sea ledges and mountains.

51
00:03:22,950 --> 00:03:27,020
Music

52
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:31,090
Music

53
00:03:31,110 --> 00:03:35,160
Music

54
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:39,230
Music

55
00:03:39,250 --> 00:03:43,280
Music

56
00:03:43,300 --> 00:03:47,330
Earth's climate engine has countless moving parts:

57
00:03:47,350 --> 00:03:51,360
tides and terrain, cross winds and currents--

58
00:03:51,380 --> 00:03:55,390
all working to equalize temperatures around

59
00:03:55,410 --> 00:03:59,400
the globe.